# Local Ollama model for the iFood agent.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
#
# Ollama defaults to a 4096-token context window. The iFood MCP server's 23 tool
# schemas alone are 10,508 tokens, so at the default the schemas are silently
# truncated and the model answers as if the tools do not exist - the same
# failure mode we hit on Gemini. num_ctx must be raised explicitly; there is no
# way to pass it through the OpenAI-compatible endpoint.
#
# USAGE
#
#   ollama pull qwen3:8b
#   ollama create ifood-agent -f Modelfile.ollama
#
# Then point .env at it:
#
#   LLM_API_KEY=ollama
#   LLM_BASE_URL=http://localhost:11434/v1
#   MODEL_NAME=ifood-agent
#
# On an 8 GB GPU the KV cache is what decides whether this fits. If the model
# spills to CPU, either lower num_ctx to 12288 or quantise the cache with
# OLLAMA_KV_CACHE_TYPE=q8_0 in the server's environment.

FROM qwen3:8b

# 16,384 tokens: the 23 tool schemas (~10.5k) plus room for a few turns.
PARAMETER num_ctx 16384

# Deterministic tool selection, matching make_client(temperature=0).
PARAMETER temperature 0
